1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 {... etc. "Shoosmith was on the right road with an early
king's side attack, whilst his opponent's forces were still undeveloped. There
were elements of success in the plan, which contained some subtle threats in
its execution; but there was just a link missing, giving Wahltuch time to
bring his reserve forces into play and to assume the offensive successfully." 
(The Field, 26 Aug 1905)} 0-1

