1. d4 {... etc. "One of the dry QP openings, which yielded, however, a pretty
ending, the only redeeming point in it. Legitimately it should have been a
draw, but Bellingham showed great skill in finding a possibility of winning in
a position which seemed perfectly even. The forces were R, N and 5Ps against
Shoosmith's R, B and 5Ps. But Bellingham, after forcing the exchange of rooks,
was able to win by bringing his K into better play, coupled with the
superiority of the N against the B." (The Field, 26 Aug 1905)} 1-0

