1. d4 d5 2. c4 e6 3. Nc3 Nf6 4. Bg5 Nbd7 5. e3 Be7 6. Nf3 O-O 7. Qc2 c6 8. Rd1
Re8 9. Bd3 dxc4 10. Bxc4 Nd5 11. Bxe7 Qxe7 12. e4 Nf4 13. g3 Ng6 14. O-O e5 15.
Be2 exd4 16. Nxd4 Nf6 17. f3 Bd7 18. Rd2 Rad8 19. Rfd1 Bc8 20. Kg2 a6 21. Na4
Nh5 22. Nb6 Qg5 23. Nxc8 Rxc8 24. Kh1 Ne7 25. f4 Qh6 26. Kg2 Nf6 27. Bf3 {
"It is but fair to note that Mr. Shoosmith was much pressed for time from this
point to his 40th move, having to make thirteen moves in about thirteen
minutes." (Howell)} g5 28. fxg5 Qxg5 29. Ne2 Ng6 30. Kh1 Ne5 31. Ng1 Nxf3 32.
Nxf3 Qe3 33. Kg2 Qxe4 34. Qxe4 Rxe4 35. h3 Rce8 36. Kf2 {"Black’s 35th move
was played to induce this, and White had no time to see this trap." (Howell)}
Ra4 37. b3 Ne4+ 38. Kg2 Nxd2 39. bxa4 Re2+ 40. Kg1 Nxf3+ {"White has lost
through time pressure, owing to taking too much time on his 21st to 25 th
moves. The game emphasises the danger of not proportioning time more evenly
over one’s moves." (Howell) Source: BCM, June 1907, p285} 0-1

